# Fixed 2026-10-01 by lane 135c (defect 135, the certain-fix audit's C9).
# Symptom: `.must()` and `.default(v)` on a value that cannot fail take a
# certain removal, and the receiver it writes was found by the last
# `.default(` in the call's text: on the compiler of `9d1c209d` a string
# argument holding `.default(` cut the call inside the string, writing
# `print(label.default("use ` with the string left open. Cause: a search of
# the text for the method's name. Now the receiver is read from the call's
# own tokens, what stands before the `.name` whose `(` the call's last `)`
# closes; the `.fixed` is this text with each call reduced to its receiver.

function main()
    label = "x"
    xs = [1, 2]
    print(label.default("use .default(v) here"))  #~ bad_operand
    print((xs.len() + 1).must())  #~ bad_operand
